  "Question": "Here is a list of the numbers of fish that Tyler caught in nine outings last summer: \\[2,0,1,3,0,3,3,1,2.\\] Which statement about the mean, mode, and median of these numbers is true?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "median \\(\\lt\\) mean \\(\\lt\\) mode",
    "B": "mean \\(\\lt\\) mode \\(\\lt\\) median",
    "C": "mean \\(\\lt\\) median \\(\\lt\\) mode",
    "D": "median \\(\\lt\\) mode \\(\\lt\\) mean",
    "E": "mode \\(\\lt\\) median \\(\\lt\\) mean"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Sorting the data makes the middle value and the repeated values easy to identify:\n\\[\n0,0,1,1,2,2,3,3,3.\n\\]\nThere are nine numbers, so the median is the fifth number, \\(2\\). The mode is \\(3\\), which appears three times, more often than any other number.\n\nThe sum is \\(15\\), so the mean is \\(15/9=5/3\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac53<2<3,\n\\]\nwhich gives mean \\(<\\) median \\(<\\) mode, choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
